 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? It depends on how thick it is. A thin layer like you did on the door can go right on with a thin layer of lacquer. A thick layer like you did on the table needs sanding, at least with 100 grit. Then hurry up. Oil paintings dry fast compared to oil based paint. You don't want cold table. You can use a thin layer of lacquer. It dries in minutes. Comes in a tiny spray can too. Stick it in your bag for emergency touch ups. It' feel smooth to the touch, and any oil residue will disappear. Rub it with your fingernail, and it should cut in.",
